--- !u!114 &1087245727
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1087245724}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The goal in <color=#3B5DC9>Rivet Rush</color> is to complete blueprints
    from the board(s) before the conveyor belt fills up completely.



    The main
    character, an assembly robot named <color=#3B5DC9>Rivet</color>, can interact
    with the chips on the conveyor belt directly in front of him. Use the <color=#3B5DC9>"Space"</color>
    key, a mouse <color=#3B5DC9>click</color>, or a <color=#3B5DC9>screen tap</color>
    to perform an action.



    -Keep an eye on the blueprints at the top of the
    screen; they indicate exactly which chips are required and the order in which
    they must be collected.

    -Press the button when the desired chip reaches
    the pickup zone in front of Rivet.

    -Let unnecessary chips pass by - they
    will loop back around.

    -Complete a blueprint according to the board to earn
    points. Successfully complete multiple blueprints in a row to earn a "streak"
    bonus.

    -Don''t make mistakes! If you grab a wrong chip or try to pick something
    up from an empty slot, Rivet will drop everything currently on his tray back
    onto the conveyor belt, and your streak will be broken.

    -The game gradually
    becomes faster and more challenging. Keep up the pace and try to score higher
    than the top players.

    -If the conveyor belt becomes completely full and
    there is no room left for a new chip, the mechanism will jam, and the game will
    end.



    <color=#3B5DC9>Types of Chips</color>



    <align=center><size=250%><sprite
    name="ChipRed"> <sprite name="ChipBlue"> <sprite name="ChipGreen"></size></align>




    <color=#3B5DC9>Coloured
    chips:</color> Red, blue, and green chips are used to complete blueprints.



    <align=center><size=250%><sprite
    name="ChipYellow"></size></align>




    Yellow chips are added to the mix later
    on.



    <align=center><size=250%><sprite name="ChipBurnt"></size></align>




    <color=#3B5DC9>Burnt
    chip:</color> This is junk that takes up space on your belt. Interact with it
    to destroy it. If your tray is empty, this action is free; however, if there
    are already chips on the tray, attempting to destroy a burnt chip will count
    as a mistake.



    <align=center><size=250%><sprite name="ChipRainbow"></size></align>




    <color=#3B5DC9>Rainbow
    chip:</color> This can act as a substitute for a chip of any colour.'
